{"term":"chill","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8f10ead938d58b0118","definition":"A moderate, but uncomfortable and penetrating coldness.","example":"There was a chill in the air.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["bechill","chilblain","chill girl","chill hours","chillish","chillness","chill-out","chillproof","chillsome","chillstep","chillth","chillwave","cook-chill","dumb chill","no chill","psychill","take the chill off","wind chill","windchill","zero chill","chilly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:58dfae6815327c9547","definition":"A sudden penetrating sense of cold, especially one that causes a brief trembling nerve response through the body; the trembling response itself; often associated with illness: fevers and chills, or susceptibility to illness.","example":"Close the window or you'll catch a chill.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["bechill","chilblain","chill girl","chill hours","chillish","chillness","chill-out","chillproof","chillsome","chillstep","chillth","chillwave","cook-chill","dumb chill","no chill","psychill","take the chill off","wind chill","windchill","zero chill","chilly"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chill#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:82bfdcd99b0d24e95b","definition":"An uncomfortable and numbing sense of fear, dread, anxiety, or alarm, often one that is sudden and usually accompanied by a trembling nerve response resembling the body's response to biting cold.","example":"Despite the heat, he felt a chill as he entered the crime scene.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"u